   <p><date when="1864-09-07">Sept,, 7<hi rend="underline"><hi rend="sup">th</hi></hi> 1864</date>.</p>
<p>His <hi rend="underline">Excelency</hi> the <hi rend="underline">Governor</hi> of <hi><orgName ref="cwgk:O001025">Kentucky</orgName></hi>.</p>
<p>We the undersigned members of <hi rend="underline">Company</hi> "C" <orgName ref="cwgk:O00011727">1<hi rend="underline"><hi rend="sup">st</hi></hi> Ky,, Light Artillery Vol</orgName>,, Having <hi rend="underline">Served</hi> for the term of <hi rend="underline">one</hi> year in the <hi rend="underline">Service</hi> of the <hi rend="underline">United</hi> <hi rend="underline">States</hi>, under <hi rend="underline">Captain</hi> <hi rend="underline">Jn</hi><hi rend="underline"><hi rend="sup">o</hi></hi> <hi rend="underline">W</hi>. <hi rend="underline">Neville</hi>, and having re-enlisted for three year's more. do respectfully petition that <hi rend="underline">Edwin</hi> <hi rend="underline">W</hi>. <hi rend="underline">Gould</hi> <hi rend="underline">Sergt</hi>,, of the above named <hi rend="underline">Company</hi> be <hi rend="underline">Appointed</hi> <hi rend="underline">Captain</hi> of the <hi rend="underline">Company</hi>. By reason that the <hi rend="underline">Captain's</hi> term of <hi rend="underline">Service</hi> expires upon the <date when="1864-09-10">tenth of <hi rend="underline">Sept</hi>,, 1864</date>. and we understand that he wishes to change his <hi rend="underline">Position</hi> or retire from service.</p>
